# Task04 structured Chat/tools and explicit Responses preparation

Status: PREPARATION_COMPLETE; implementation, offline/native/paid qualification and capability readiness **NOT_RUN**. Whole04/full03/all17 remain incomplete. This is a bounded follow-on contract packet, not a superseding architecture, approval to spend, production-root entry, or acceptance of the mutable first Gateway helper. Accepted PURE and B C2 stay unchanged in this preparation. The compiled production manifest is EMPTY. Current B admits only its narrow plain Chat and default single-value embedding envelopes. New capability construction must remain denied until independently accepted bounds, results, terminal recipes and actual qualification exist.

Read-only inspection used repository instructions, the original goal/tasks04/05/07/08/09, authoritative decision-gates/architecture, existing dispatch/cost/doc/token-review/ledger preparation, accepted terminal-capture C2 design and installed official sources. Exact hashes and line locators are in source-evidence.json. No network, credentials, services, targets, models, Git operations, dependency installation, product edits, existing QA edits or application tests. Only this new two-file packet is a deliverable; scratch belongs exclusively to work/resume/task04-structured-gateway-preparation/. Source observations are not acceptance; refresh affected fingerprints before implementation.

## Source-grounded boundaries

Official @convex-dev/ai-sdk-provider0.2.1 uses Chat from @ai-sdk/openai-compatible3.0.14 and **its nested @ai-sdk/openai4.0.45** for Responses, rather than the separately installed root OpenAI4.0.83. AI7.0.127/provider4.0.21 native calls are v4. Qualify the module actually resolved by Gateway and record all dependency/transitive-transform hashes. Gateway has no public injected fetch: gatewayFetch obtains getServiceToken then replaces Authorization. Offline wire fixtures must use underlying official factories' supported injected-fetch seam with in-memory responses; production remains official Gateway, no global fetch patch, custom transport, direct upstream key/provider fallback or Vercel @ai-sdk/gateway substitution.

Chat conversion collapses a single user text part to a string but multiple user parts become an array; assistant text parts concatenate, tool calls serialize input with JSON.stringify, tool results become separate messages with tool_call_id and output-dependent serialization. Tool definitions map name/description/inputSchema/strict and toolChoice maps auto/none/required/specific name. Native responseFormat maps schema/name/default response/description and strictJsonSchema default true to response_format.json_schema; maxOutputTokens becomes max_tokens. Provider option passthrough exists, so deny unknown options **before** projection. supportsStructuredOutputs:true merely enables serialization, not actual model or schema compatibility.

Explicit Responses uses provider-qualified model rewriting after conversion and an inner default-settings middleware for openai.store:false. The governed canonical native request must already include that pinned false value. Its conversion depends on model capability/system mode and store, reconstructs function_call arguments and function_call_output, and can use provider metadata to reference prior items. Stateless support must deny those references and reconstruct complete inputs. ResponseFormat becomes text.format with schema/name/default response/description/strict; maxOutputTokens becomes max_output_tokens. Ordinary custom backend function tools are supported; provider-hosted tools, deferLoading/allowedCallers/output_schema options and other native extensions must remain outside the first reviewed envelope unless separately proved. Tool output_schema specifically changes function output encoding: do not introduce it implicitly.

Both installed Chat and Responses stream converters emit native finish during flush. Chat raw usage may be absent despite mapped zero component counts. Responses distinguishes raw response.completed/incomplete/failed; EOF alone can synthesize a finish without any genuine upstream terminal event. includeRawChunks:true is a supported server-only observation seam; inspect raw transiently and never persist/deliver it. Responses does not invoke Chat's convexGateway cost extractor. Source comments about dollar costs, model aliases and docs are candidate semantic evidence, not actual complete currency/charge/readiness receipts.

## Minimal follow-on contracts and ownership

Proceed only after accepted B C2 native qualification **and verified target retirement**, followed by the independently accepted terminal-capture C2 implementation/native extension. Do not mutate the frozen qualification target or roll unrelated work into it. Repair/accept the current helper's deadline/cancellation lifecycle separately; this packet does not inspect or judge its mutable source.

1. Freeze a **compiled backend envelope registry** for each operation/model/interface/recipe revision. It owns exact prompts, schema, schema name/description/defaults/strictness, tool definitions/choice, allowed native roles/parts/output forms and bounded cardinalities/bytes. Bind registry hash into existing schemaVersion/toolRegistryVersion/promptVersion/extractionVersion and root proof identities. Tenant policies may narrow; tenant/JWT/client claims cannot install definitions, prices or proofs. No client closure execution. Initially fixed toolChoice and schema metadata can be reconstructed from immutable registry pins, without changing PURE. Deny all mismatches instead of silently deleting knobs. If variable toolChoice/name/description/strict defaults are genuinely needed, propose a minimal separately reviewed PURE identity extension first; never make source projection lossy.
2. Extend B's compiled QualifiedDispatchEvidence rule/envelope unions and deterministic deriveQualifiedInputBound dispatch, keeping unchanged strict PURE U/M/context rules. Add only accepted operation-specific recipes; absent recipe remains unavailable. B owns bootstrap/root validation, terminal-source validation and private-result validators; C owns final-native normalization/reconstruction and wrappers. Request proof binds **complete detached final native shapes** to root, source transforms, documents, registry/prompt/schema/tool versions and checkedAt/expiry/revocation. Exact canonical equality is checked alongside hashes at admission/checkpoint/replay. Legacy narrow recipes remain exactly narrow; no default proof applied to tools/schema/Responses.
Keep PURE's unique qualification per model/interface and B's unique dispatchEvidence per receiptId. Do not add several operation-specific qualification rows with the same model/interface and hope resolution selects one. The smallest compatible backend extension is one reviewed receipt/evidence entry whose compiled finite subrecipe registry selects by snapshot.operationKey plus pinned schema/tool/prompt versions, with exact uniqueness and deny-on-missing selection. Its qualified capability union, priceRevision/boundRevision and K cover every enabled subrecipe; if any lacks proof it cannot be enabled. Checkpoint reselects the same subrecipe; native method identity distinguishes generate/stream where proofs differ. This preserves PURE and requires B evidence validation/derive call sites to receive trusted snapshot/operation pins rather than request-supplied selectors.
3. Add versioned **typed private result variants** for structured extraction/conflict, tool turns and explicit Responses in B's canonical private string, checked against stored operation/interface/registry/input identity. Preserve current legacy plain-text/embedding result behavior. No new table/index required for typed JSON; runtimePolicySchema changes only if a separately justified field is needed. Terminal capture C2's two optional attempt fields and two internal mutations remain its accepted ownership, not an outbox/worker proposal. Do not revive the superseded outbox design in older ledger preparation.
4. C normalizes/validates the final AI-native params, submits flat canonical ModelCallRequest, and reconstructs the exact detached admitted native call. B internally retains PURE {snapshot,request}; never send that envelope as requestCanonical. Every automatic Agent step and MemoryModel extraction/conflict/secondary call has one native governed child under same run/request and tenant accounts, checkpoint before service-token lookup, maxRetries:0 and no caller model/prepareStep replacement. Official constructor readiness alone is insufficient. Default embedding stays deterministic single-value children in accepted B despite provider maximum512, exact profile1536 dimensions and stable absolute offsets.
5. After acceptance of these contracts and actual capability proofs, wire the two runtimeMemory injection sites and remove its unavailable adapter stub in a separate step, preserving all current grant/source/commit fences. Task05 freezes executable agent definitions/canonical transcript/run parents; Task07 owns typed tool/execution status, event persistence and effect deduplication; Task08 owns extraction/conflict source lineage/version commits, watermarks/tombstones; Task09 owns remote TS/UI observation. A helper alone is neither memory functionality nor full no-bypass closure.

Affected proposed files: B runtimeModelPolicyBootstrap.ts (rule/result/terminal evidence interfaces; production registry remains empty pending actual review), runtimeModelPolicy.ts (derive/validate/capture-result/replay gates), runtimePolicySchema.ts only the accepted terminal-capture fields unless a later review proves more necessary, existing model-policy-admission.test.ts plus actual native fixtures after freeze; C runtimeGateway.ts and gateway-dispatch.test.ts, then new gateway-memory-adapter.test.ts and separately scoped runtimeMemory.ts/runtimeMemoryServices.ts wiring. PURE src/domain/model-policy.ts stays unchanged for fixed registry defaults. A new backend-only registry module is a routine ownership choice, named at freeze; it must not become a browser export or public registration. Existing extraction/conflict domain files change only if a separately reviewed bounded schema/validator is required. Generated API changes use authorized official codegen later, never hand edits. All changed registered functions enter actual inventory/visibility/auth qualification. No new registered proxy to control-plane capture or root installation.

## Full request identity and trusted tool contracts

Bind ordered system/user/assistant/tool roles and every admitted part, normalized scalar text, tool call IDs/names/inputs, result IDs/names/output discriminators and complete payloads, exact schema own-key spelling (including own JSON __proto__), complete tool definitions, options/defaults, native interface/model, semantic/source/content revision, parent/child/step/batch and registry pins. Reject accessors, symbols, sparse arrays, nonfinite numbers, nonplain JSON, ill-formed Unicode, message/part/tool/provider metadata, headers/routing, unknown top-level keys and mutable objects before any awaits. Normalize text exactly under existing NFC/LF/trim contract; do not normalize arbitrary JSON keys/tool IDs/schema strings by accident. Fixed definition texts are serialized exactly as compiled; their counted bytes and identity must match dispatched bytes. Registry lookup compares exact definition/default bytes, not merely matching tool names.

PURE already binds tool.definition and outputSchema unknown canonical records, plus ordered roles/tool-call/results. It lacks explicit variable responseFormat name/description/toolChoice fields. Fix those through pinned immutable backend registry defaults and runtime equality checks; never accept a supplied different value and discard it. Tool-result.output's record can losslessly bind the v4 output discriminator/value; allow only compiled text/json/error-text/error-json/denial shapes needed by that tool, and validate semantics before encoding. Exclude media/content provider outputs until separately reviewed. Match calls/results by IDs/names with bounded no-orphan/no-duplicate ordering; trusted transcript adapter determines prior-turn unresolved calls and approval state. Pairing validator must not reject a legitimate staged tool call merely because its result belongs to the next native step. No synthetic tool authorization from prompt, memory, model output or a caller tool ID.

Each trusted tool registry entry declares bounded input schema and strict runtime validator, backend executor identity/version, grants/source-currentness, operation ID, side-effect/approval/retry semantics and bounded output schema/validator/serialization. Validate every generated call before invoking its executor. An invalid model tool call may still be a charged terminal, never an authorized effect. Use stable tool-effect IDs and persist visibility/effect evidence before future fallback decisions. Tool result observation and source eligibility are distinct: only verified tool results under source policy may feed memory; secrets/internal context/raw reasoning never become public transcript or authoritative user facts. Tool definitions and outputs increase **next-call** U even if tool execution itself is free. Any tool which performs billable inference must use its own child admission; no secondary bypass.

## Structured extraction and conflict results

Use AI7 Output.object with a compiled schema/runtime validator through the governed native model. Its native responseFormat only asks the provider for JSON; AI partial structured output is explicitly not fully validated. Partial/malformed/truncated/refusal output never becomes a committed fact/conflict decision. Capture actual terminal charge independently, then validate complete result and attach only if eligible. No hidden retry on Output.object parse failure: a model call already occurred. MemoryModel.extract returns the validated facts object; source-aware parseSourceFactsResponse rechecks role/eligibility and assigns exact lineage. It must not silently substitute legacy permissive parsing.

FACTS_JSON_SCHEMA has nested arrays/string fields without max cardinality/length; fullValue is optional. Strict provider schema acceptance and finite serialized result bounds therefore remain unqualified. Compile a versioned bounded transport schema: pin facts/tags/entities/relations maxima and scalar byte/length limits consistent with the chosen source envelope and consumer semantics; prove corresponding strict runtime validation and finite canonical byte envelope. OpenAI strict-schema requirements may require every property required and optional domain values represented as nullable transport values. Such a conversion must be explicit, schema-versioned, lossless at domain boundary and offline/live qualified; do not send the current schema and claim strict acceptance from a source flag. Finite limits are implementation choices only when all allowed input/output behavior remains meaningful; an unavoidably inadequate source/output envelope is a consequential conflict to report.

facts.resolve has ConflictDecision action UPDATE|SUPERSEDE|NONE|ADD, targetFactId/mergedFact nullable, reason, optional confidence0..100; no existing transport JSON schema constant. Compile a bounded strict schema, represent optional confidence deterministically under a pinned mapping, and validate complete structure before domain validateConflictDecision. UPDATE/SUPERSEDE targets must belong to the pinned scoped existing-fact set; UPDATE requires mergedFact. Input prompt identity includes candidate, exact fact IDs/revisions and prompt options. MemoryModel.resolve currently provides only system/prompt/candidate, without a typed existing-facts snapshot. Freeze a trusted Task08 lookup/binding seam carrying the exact scoped existing-fact IDs/revisions to schema/result validation; never infer authority or currentness by parsing caller prompt text. If a typed MemoryModel contract addition is necessary, scope src/domain/contracts.ts and its real consumers explicitly in that separate freeze. Replay requires current source/fact versions; a previously charged obsolete decision may be retained privately but cannot commit a belief update. This internal belief-conflict function does not add excluded Decisions/Jev APIs. Task08 atomically compares revisions/order/tombstones on commit; model correctness is never authority for replacing newer beliefs.

